L309: #### Sample-based estimators of the UBSR gradient.
L310: Let $\theta\in\Theta$ and $m\in\mathbb{N}$. Let $Z^{\theta}$ denote the random variable associated with the trajectories induced by policy $\pi_{\theta}$. Precisely, $Z^{\theta}$ takes values in $\mathcal{T}$ under the distribution $p_{\theta}$. Let $Z_{1},Z_{2},\ldots,Z_{m}$ and $\hat{Z}_{1},\hat{Z}_{2},\ldots,\hat{Z}_{m}$ be $2m$ i.i.d. copies of $Z^{\theta}$.
L311: Let $\tau_{1},\tau_{2},\ldots,\tau_{m}$ and $\hat{\tau}_{1},\hat{\tau}_{2},\ldots,\hat{\tau}_{m}$ be $m$ realizations each from $Z_{1},Z_{2},\ldots,Z_{m}$ and $\hat{Z}_{1},\hat{Z}_{2},\ldots,\hat{Z}_{m}$, respectively, i.e., $\tau_{i}\sim Z_{i},\hat{\tau}_{i}\sim\hat{Z}_{i},\forall i$.
L312: We use the shorthand notation $\mathbf{z},\mathbf{\hat{z}}$ to denote the $m$ realizations as an $m$-dimensional vector, and use $\mathbf{Z},\mathbf{\hat{Z}}$ to denote the $m$ random variables as an $m$-dimensional random vector.
L313: Formally, $\mathbf{z}\triangleq\langle\tau_{1},\tau_{2},\ldots,\tau_{m}\rangle,\mathbf{z}\triangleq\langle\hat{\tau}_{1},\hat{\tau}_{2},\ldots,\hat{\tau}_{m}\rangle,\mathbf{Z}\triangleq\langle Z_{1},Z_{2},\ldots,Z_{m}\rangle$, and $\mathbf{\hat{Z}}\triangleq\langle\hat{Z}_{1},\hat{Z}_{2},\ldots,\hat{Z}_{m}\rangle$.
L314: Then $\srd_{\theta}^{m}:\mathcal{T}^{m}\to\mathbb{R}$ and $Q_{\theta}^{m}:\mathcal{T}^{m}\times\mathcal{T}^{m}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}$ are our proposed estimators of $\srd(\theta)$ and $\nabla\srd(\theta)$ respectively, given by
L315:  | $\displaystyle\srd_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{z}\right)$  | $\displaystyle=\inf\left\{k\in\mathbb{R}\left|\frac{1}{m}\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{m}l(c(\mathbf{z}_{j})-k)\leq\lambda\right.\right\},$  |
L316:  | $\displaystyle Q_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{\hat{z}},\mathbf{z}\right)$  | $\displaystyle=\frac{\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{m}{l\left(c(\mathbf{z}_{j})-\srd_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{z}\right)\right)g(\theta,\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{j})}}{\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{m}l^{\prime}\left(c(\mathbf{z}_{j})-\srd_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{z}\right)\right)}.$  |  | (22)
L317: Next, we derive error bounds on the estimator $Q_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}},\mathbf{Z}\right)$
L318: ###### Lemma 3.
L319: 
L320: Suppose the loss function is convex and strictly-increasing, and cite95†assumptions (A8) , cite96†(A9) and cite99†(A10) are satisfied. Suppose there exists $\hat{\sigma_{1}}>0$ such that for every $\theta\in\Theta,\mathrm{Var}(l^{\prime}(-F-\srd(\theta_{)}))\leq\hat{\sigma_{1}}^{2}$. Then,
L321:  | $\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left\lVert\nabla\srd(\theta)-Q_{\theta}^{m}\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}},\mathbf{Z}\right)\right\rVert_{2}^{2}\right]$  | $\displaystyle\leq\frac{3\sigma_{g}^{2}K_{1}}{b_{1}^{2}m},$  |
L322: where $K_{1}=4\sigma_{1}^{2}+3\lambda^{2}+B_{1}^{2}\left(C_{2}+\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}}{b_{1}^{2}m}\right)+\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2}\hat{\sigma_{1}}^{2}}{b_{1}^{2}}$, and the constants $b_{1},B_{1}$ are as defined in cite95†assumption (A8) , and $\sigma_{1},\sigma_{g}$ are as defined in cite96†assumptions (A9) and cite99†(A10) respectively.
